# Companion navbar — protected (floating chips + VRM-stable mount)

**User-confirmed good state (2026-08-22).** Soft look before *and after* avatar load. Do not reintroduce a filled plate.

## Invariants

| Area | Rule |
|------|------|
| Layout | Floating chips only (`NAV_CHIP` on buttons). Outer navbar `Container` must **not** set `backgroundOpacity`, `backgroundColor`, or filled plate props |
| Mount | `Stage` wraps **only** `{children}` in `<Suspense>`. `<Navbar />` is a **sibling outside** that Suspense so VRM `useLoader` suspend does not remount the bar |
| Frost | `CompanionNavbarFrost` stays a no-op stub (`() => null`). No full-bleed DOM frost strip |
| Soft glass elsewhere | Settings dialog / Providers cards may keep soft opacity (~0.65–0.68). That is **not** the bottom bar |

## Forbidden without explicit user request

- Putting a translucent/opaque filled plate behind the whole bottom navbar
- Moving `<Navbar />` inside the Stage (or `_app`) Suspense that wraps VRM/scene children
- Re-enabling DOM frost / full-bleed blur strip under the bar
- “Fixing” dark-on-VRM by cranking panel `backgroundOpacity` back toward 1 on a filled plate

## Why

VRM load suspends via `useLoader`. If the nearest Suspense wraps the whole `Outlet`/`Stage`, Navbar remounts and a plate/slab look returns after avatar load.

